Description: IREE model compiler with the Rockchip RK3588 NPU (Rocket) target
 rocket-compiler compiles ONNX-imported MLIR models into IREE .vmfb modules
 that run convolutions, matmuls, pooling and elementwise work on the RK3588
 NPU through the mainline "rocket" accel driver, and everything else on the
 CPU. It also explains, per operation, why each candidate did or did not
 offload (the "audit" subcommand).
 .
 The package carries its own build of IREE's libIREECompiler.so with the
 Rocket target plugin compiled in, plus the iree-lld linker it needs, in a
 private directory. Neither is meant to be used by anything else, and
 neither conflicts with an upstream IREE installation.
 .
 Compiling does not need the NPU, so the package is useful on a desktop
 that cross-compiles models for the board. Running the modules needs the
 IREE runtime with the Rocket HAL driver, which is not part of this package.
